# Real per-view URLs (react-router-dom's BrowserRouter) mean a direct hit or a
# refresh on a deep path like /fleet has no matching static file, so each route
# has to be rewritten to an HTML file explicitly. All rewrites (200), no redirects.
#
# The public pages get their own prerendered files (scripts/prerender-public.mjs)
# so crawlers see the right title, canonical and text for each. Every signed-in
# route and /login get app.html, the plain app shell. "/" needs no rule: it is
# dist/index.html, the prerendered landing page.
#
# There is deliberately no "/* /index.html 200" catch-all any more. It answered
# made-up paths with a 200 and the home page's content, which Google indexes as a
# "soft 404". A route missing from this list now gets the 404 page, so a new
# route in App.jsx needs a line here too.
#
# Netlify functions at /.netlify/functions/* resolve before these rules.
/terms      /terms.html     200
/privacy    /privacy.html   200
/training   /training.html  200

/login      /app.html  200
/dashboard  /app.html  200
